**Rotation summary through day 4 (Fri 2026-09-04)**

**Pages so far**

- **p-001 (day 1, Tue 09-01, 22:10 UTC) search_latency_high, warning — DISMISSED.** search-service p95 67ms baseline → 75-84ms peak while request_count went 1450 → 2785 (evening ramp); back to ~68ms by 22:00. error_rate ~0.006, cpu ~0.40, memory ~0.62 all flat; logs only CACHE_HIT + 2 QUERY_SLOW. No deploys. Ruled out `config-day01-search-service` (search.log_level info→debug, 16:10 UTC) because latency tracked traffic, not the 16:10 change.
- **p-002 (day 2, Wed 09-02, 22:10 UTC) inventory_latency_high, warning — DISMISSED.** p95 ~90ms → ~105ms peak as request_count 730 → 1440, back to 90ms by 22:00; error_rate ~0.004, cpu ~0.25, dep latency flat; only STOCK_READ + 3 QUERY_SLOW logs. Ruled out `deploy-day02-order-service` (v2.3.1 tax-rounding) — wrong service/mechanism.
- **p-003 (day 3, Thu 09-03, 15:20 UTC) search_latency_high, warning — DISMISSED.** Pure noise: p95 stayed in its normal 64-77ms band all day (69.9ms at 15:15), request_count steady ~1500, everything flat, zero changes since Sep 1.
- **p-004 (day 3, Thu 09-03, 22:10 UTC) notification_latency_high, warning — DISMISSED.** p95 198 → 225ms peak while send volume 440 → 854; Courierly dependency_latency 250 → 280ms; error_rate ~0.008 flat; all vendor_snapshots that day had changed=False; no errors in logs.
- **p-005 (day 4, Fri 09-04, 19:05 UTC) checkout_error_rate_high, CRITICAL — RESOLVED, cause `config-day04-reduce`.** Sharp onset exactly at 19:00 UTC: payment-orchestrator connection_pool_utilization 0.22 → 0.99, connection_pool_wait_ms 12 → ~4800, checkout-api error_rate 0.005 → 0.18, p95 300ms → 5200ms, 61 × CONNECTION_POOL_TIMEOUT errors in checkout-api logs. Cause: `config-day04-reduce` (cost-optimizer, 09:00 UTC) payments.max_connections 100 → 20; impact appeared ~10h later as load/connection churn caught up. Ruled out `deploy-day04-decoy` (checkout-api v4.18.0, 18:40 UTC, analytics-banner/checkout-copy only) — cosmetic, cannot exhaust the payments DB pool. Note payment_success_rate stayed ~0.996 (PayRail fine) — failure was internal pool starvation. Fixed by `config-day04-restore` (12:25 PT / 19:25 UTC, back to 100) + `action-day04-recycle` pod recycle; alert resolved 19:28 UTC.
- **p-006 (day 4, Fri 09-04, 22:10 UTC) order_latency_high, warning — DISMISSED.** order-service p95 flat 123-138ms, error_rate ~0.003, cpu ~0.21, traffic declining 1150 → 770. Prior checkout incident already resolved at 19:28 and never touched order-service.

**Recurring patterns / heuristics learned**

- There is a **recurring 22:10 UTC (15:10 PT) "…_latency_high" warning** that fires on a rotating service (search, inventory, notification, order). Every instance so far has been benign: p95 rises ~15-30% in lockstep with the evening request_count ramp (often ~2x), while error_rate, cpu, memory and dependency_latency stay flat, logs show only INFO codes plus a couple of QUERY_SLOW, and it auto-resolves ~22:35. Default posture: dismiss, but always verify flat error_rate + traffic correlation first.
- **Real incidents look different:** step-function onset at a single minute, error_rate jumping 30x+, p95 10x+, plus a matching ERROR log code (e.g. CONNECTION_POOL_TIMEOUT), and severity=critical.
- **Checks that pay off (cheap, in this order):** (1) one pivoted metrics query with `max(CASE WHEN signal=...)` over the service ± its dependency, comparing p95 vs request_count vs error_rate; (2) `logs GROUP BY service, level, code` for the window — any ERROR row is the tell; (3) union of deployments + config_changes in the last ~36h; (4) vendor_snapshots filtered on `changed = true` (all-operational rows are pure noise, thousands of duplicates).
- Metrics are 15-min normally but switch to **per-minute granularity around incidents** (e.g. from 18:00 UTC on day 4), so wide time ranges blow the 50-row limit — filter `minute(event_time) IN (0,15,30,45)` or narrow the window.
- Baseline p95 by service: checkout-api ~280-300ms, order-service ~125-135ms, notification-worker ~200ms (Courierly dep ~250ms), inventory-service ~90ms, search-service ~70ms. Typical error rates: checkout 0.005, payment-orch 0.004, order 0.003, inventory 0.004, search 0.006, notification 0.008. payment_success_rate ~0.996.
- `runbooks` returned nothing for search/latency queries; `past_incidents` advice can be stale (e.g. INC-176 blames search GC pauses at p99 > 2s — did not match our mild warnings).
- Deploy/config events are named suggestively (`deploy-day04-decoy`) — do not rely on names; match mechanism and timing.

**Open/standing context for later pages**

- Still in effect: search.log_level = debug on search-service since 09-01 (no observed impact); order-service v2.3.1 tax-rounding (09-02); inventory-service v8.0.4 "Serve stock reads with stale-while-revalidate" (deployed 09-03 23:05 UTC) — watch for stale-stock/oversell symptoms; checkout-api v4.18.0 (09-04).
- A "cost-optimizer" actor made the day-4 breaking config change; treat future cost-optimizer config edits (pool sizes, limits, timeouts) as prime suspects, and note their impact can lag hours behind the change.

